{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794760633425,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd9ffeEQ4EaGVDFSUKgQ","part":{"id":"prt_1e011ec51001xQkEewdu9qVhbw","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd9ffeEQ4EaGVDFSUKgQ","messageID":"msg_1e011e3180017Qq9TyOxRdMBIB","type":"step-start","snapshot":"cb2dd1a8cf0b094b21ed2902f929f310166425cb"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794760635734,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd9ffeEQ4EaGVDFSUKgQ","part":{"partID":"prt_1e011f0a3002AT8zlFDMa5ZDR0","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd9ffeEQ4EaGVDFSUKgQ","messageID":"msg_1e011e3180017Qq9TyOxRdMBIB","type":"tool","id":"call_117fcc14be1b417783067223","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"step_create_state_log\" -A 60 .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml | head -120"},"output":"556:          open_run: \"Run step_create_state_log.command unchanged. With the hand-written log set aside, it opens the run from the moved config.\"\n557-          replay_command: |\n558-            GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n559-            [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n560-            RUN_DIR=\"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\"\n561-            node -e '\n562-              const fs = require(\"fs\"), os = require(\"os\"), path = require(\"path\");\n563-              const { spawnSync } = require(\"child_process\");\n564-              const [gateway, legacyLog, runDir] = process.argv.slice(1);\n565-              let replayedIterations = 0;\n566-              let keptOnlyInLegacyLog = 0;\n567-              for (const line of fs.readFileSync(legacyLog, \"utf8\").split(\"\\n\")) {\n568-                if (line.trim() === \"\") continue;\n569-                let row;\n570-                try { row = JSON.parse(line); } catch { keptOnlyInLegacyLog += 1; continue; }\n571-                // The run open already replaced the config row.\n572-                if (row && row.type === \"config\") continue;\n573-                if (!row || row.type !== \"iteration\") { keptOnlyInLegacyLog += 1; continue; }\n574-                const tempDir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"deep-review-replay-\"));\n575-                const eventFile = path.join(tempDir, \"row.json\");\n576-                fs.writeFileSync(eventFile, JSON.stringify(row));\n577-                const result = spawnSync(process.execPath, [gateway, \"--mode\", \"review\", \"--run-directory\", runDir, \"--event-json\", eventFile], { encoding: \"utf8\" });\n578-                fs.rmSync(tempDir, { recursive: true, force: true });\n579-                if (result.status === 2) { process.stdout.write(result.stdout || \"\"); process.exit(2); }\n580-                if (result.status === 0) replayedIterations += 1; else keptOnlyInLegacyLog += 1;\n581-              }\n582-              process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify({ replayedIterations, keptOnlyInLegacyLog, legacyLog }) + \"\\n\");\n583-            ' \"$GATEWAY\" \"$RUN_DIR/deep-review-state.legacy.jsonl\" \"$RUN_DIR\"\n584-        on_completed_session:\n585-          before_append: \"Run on_moved_legacy_state first when it applies.\"\n586-          log: \"Prior session already completed. Either archive the completed review/ tree and start a fresh session, or jump straight to synthesis with the existing artifacts.\"\n587-          skip_to: phase_synthesis\n588-        on_invalid_state:\n589-          halt: true\n590-          release_lock: step_release_lock\n591-          message: \"Existing deep-review state in review/ is incomplete or contradictory. Repair or archive the invalid review packet before continuing.\"\n592-        on_fresh:\n593-          action: \"Proceed with a new session\"\n594-\n595-      step_scope_discovery:\n596-        action: \"Resolve review target to a concrete file list based on target type\"\n597-        resolve:\n598-          spec-folder: |\n599-            1. Inspect spec.md, plan.md, tasks.md, acceptance-criteria.md, implementation-summary.md, and goal-file-manifest.txt when present\n600-            2. If goal-file-manifest.txt exists, parse one repo-relative path per non-empty, non-comment line; reject absolute paths, traversal outside repo_root, duplicates, missing paths, and non-file entries\n601-            3. Fail before dispatch with line-numbered validation errors when any manifest entry is invalid; otherwise set scope = the validated manifest paths in declared order\n602-            4. When no manifest exists, discover implementation files referenced in the canonical spec artifacts\n603-            5. Discover test files associated with the implementation files\n604-            6. Set scope = all discovered implementation and test files\n605-          skill: |\n606-            1. Read SKILL.md from .skilled/skills/{skill_name}/\n607-            2. Discover references/, assets/, scripts/ contents\n608-            3. Find agent definitions referencing this skill across runtimes\n609-            4. Find command entry points referencing this skill\n610-            5. Set scope = all discovered files\n611-          agent: |\n612-            1. Find agent definition across repo-managed runtimes (.claude/agents/, .skilled/agents/)\n613-            2. Compare agent definitions for consistency\n614-            3. Set scope = all discovered agent files\n615-          track: |\n616-            1. List all child spec folders under specs/{track}/ or .opencode/specs/{track}/\n--\n720:      step_create_state_log:\n721-        action: \"Open the run in the ledger: record deep_review.run_initialized through the append gateway, which writes the state log's first row\"\n722-        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n723-        note: |\n724-          The state log is a projection the gateway rebuilds from the ledger, so this step never writes\n725-          it directly. A config row written beside the ledger carries keys the projection cannot\n726-          rebuild, and the projection refuses to drop them, so every later append in the run would\n727-          commit to the ledger and then exit 2. Recording the run's opening as a ledger event makes\n728-          the projected config row the state log's first row from the start. The full config stays\n729-          in deep-review-config.json, which is what the reducer reads.\n730-        command: |\n731-          GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n732-          [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n733-          EVENT_FILE=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-run-open.XXXXXX\")\"\n734-          node -e '\n735-            const fs = require(\"fs\"), crypto = require(\"crypto\");\n736-            const [configPath, workflowPath] = process.argv.slice(1);\n737-            const sha = (bytes) => crypto.createHash(\"sha256\").update(bytes).digest(\"hex\");\n738-            const raw = fs.readFileSync(configPath);\n739-            const config = JSON.parse(raw);\n740-            const targetTypes = { files: \"file\", file: \"file\", directory: \"directory\", \"spec-folder\": \"directory\", track: \"directory\", repository: \"repository\" };\n741-            const lineageModes = { new: \"fresh\", fresh: \"fresh\", restart: \"restart\", resume: \"resume\" };\n742-            // The projected config row shows this topic; one the schema cannot hold is left out,\n743-            // and the row falls back to the run id rather than the run failing to open.\n744-            const topic = typeof config.topic === \"string\" && config.topic.trim() !== \"\" && config.topic.length <= 4096\n745-              ? config.topic\n746-              : null;\n747-            process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify({\n748-              stem: \"deep_review.run_initialized\",\n749-              scope: { runId: config.sessionId, sessionId: config.sessionId, generation: Number(config.generation) || 1 },\n750-              data: {\n751-                target: {\n752-                  targetId: \"review-target\",\n753-                  targetType: targetTypes[config.reviewTargetType] || \"artifact\",\n754-                  artifactRef: \"deep-review-config.json#reviewTarget\",\n755-                  sourceDigest: sha(String(config.reviewTarget)),\n756-                  contentDigest: sha(raw),\n757-                },\n758-                lineageMode: lineageModes[config.lineageMode] || \"fresh\",\n759-                maxIterations: Number(config.maxIterations),\n760-                convergencePolicyVersion: \"convergence-policy@\" + ((config.antiConvergence && config.antiConvergence.convergenceMode) || \"default\"),\n761-                reviewModeContractDigest: sha(fs.readFileSync(workflowPath)),\n762-                initialReleaseReadinessState: \"not-assessed\",\n763-                ...(topic === null ? {} : { topic }),\n764-              },\n765-            }));\n766-          ' \"{state_paths.config}\" \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml\" > \"$EVENT_FILE\" || { rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"; exit 1; }\n767-          node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n768-          STATUS=$?\n769-          rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n770-          exit \"$STATUS\"\n771-        output: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n772-\n773-      step_record_restarted_run:\n774-        skip_when: \"lineage_mode != 'restart'\"\n775-        action: \"Record the restarted lineage after the run-open row so the restart marker never precedes deep_review.run_initialized\"\n776-        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n777-        append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.run_restarted\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}},\"data\":{\"priorTailDigest\":\"{prior_tail_digest}\",\"archivedLineageId\":\"{prior_session_id}\",\"restartReason\":\"Restart requested: the prior review packet was archived and a new lineage segment opened.\",\"continuedFromRunId\":\"{prior_session_id}-i{iteration_count}\",\"compatibilityDecision\":\"exact\",\"recoveryReceiptRef\":\"none\"}}'\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"556:          open_run: \"Run step_create_state_log.command unchanged. With the hand-written log set aside, it opens the run from the moved config.\"\n557-          replay_command: |\n558-            GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n559-            [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n560-            RUN_DIR=\"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\"\n561-            node -e '\n562-              const fs = require(\"fs\"), os = require(\"os\"), path = require(\"path\");\n563-              const { spawnSync } = require(\"child_process\");\n564-              const [gateway, legacyLog, runDir] = process.argv.slice(1);\n565-              let replayedIterations = 0;\n566-              let keptOnlyInLegacyLog = 0;\n567-              for (const line of fs.readFileSync(legacyLog, \"utf8\").split(\"\\n\")) {\n568-                if (line.trim() === \"\") continue;\n569-                let row;\n570-                try { row = JSON.parse(line); } catch { keptOnlyInLegacyLog += 1; continue; }\n571-                // The run open already replaced the config row.\n572-                if (row && row.type === \"config\") continue;\n573-                if (!row || row.type !== \"iteration\") { keptOnlyInLegacyLog += 1; continue; }\n574-                const tempDir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"deep-review-replay-\"));\n575-                const eventFile = path.join(tempDir, \"row.json\");\n576-                fs.writeFileSync(eventFile, JSON.stringify(row));\n577-                const result = spawnSync(process.execPath, [gateway, \"--mode\", \"review\", \"--run-directory\", runDir, \"--event-json\", eventFile], { encoding: \"utf8\" });\n578-                fs.rmSync(tempDir, { recursive: true, force: true });\n579-                if (result.status === 2) { process.stdout.write(result.stdout || \"\"); process.exit(2); }\n580-                if (result.status === 0) replayedIterations += 1; else keptOnlyInLegacyLog += 1;\n581-              }\n582-              process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify({ replayedIterations, keptOnlyInLegacyLog, legacyLog }) + \"\\n\");\n583-            ' \"$GATEWAY\" \"$RUN_DIR/deep-review-state.legacy.jsonl\" \"$RUN_DIR\"\n584-        on_completed_session:\n585-          before_append: \"Run on_moved_legacy_state first when it applies.\"\n586-          log: \"Prior session already completed. Either archive the completed review/ tree and start a fresh session, or jump straight to synthesis with the existing artifacts.\"\n587-          skip_to: phase_synthesis\n588-        on_invalid_state:\n589-          halt: true\n590-          release_lock: step_release_lock\n591-          message: \"Existing deep-review state in review/ is incomplete or contradictory. Repair or archive the invalid review packet before continuing.\"\n592-        on_fresh:\n593-          action: \"Proceed with a new session\"\n594-\n595-      step_scope_discovery:\n596-        action: \"Resolve review target to a concrete file list based on target type\"\n597-        resolve:\n598-          spec-folder: |\n599-            1. Inspect spec.md, plan.md, tasks.md, acceptance-criteria.md, implementation-summary.md, and goal-file-manifest.txt when present\n600-            2. If goal-file-manifest.txt exists, parse one repo-relative path per non-empty, non-comment line; reject absolute paths, traversal outside repo_root, duplicates, missing paths, and non-file entries\n601-            3. Fail before dispatch with line-numbered validation errors when any manifest entry is invalid; otherwise set scope = the validated manifest paths in declared order\n602-            4. When no manifest exists, discover implementation files referenced in the canonical spec artifacts\n603-            5. Discover test files associated with the implementation files\n604-            6. Set scope = all discovered implementation and test files\n605-          skill: |\n606-            1. Read SKILL.md from .skilled/skills/{skill_name}/\n607-            2. Discover references/, assets/, scripts/ contents\n608-            3. Find agent definitions referencing this skill across runtimes\n609-            4. Find command entry points referencing this skill\n610-            5. Set scope = all discovered files\n611-          agent: |\n612-            1. Find agent definition across repo-managed runtimes (.claude/agents/, .skilled/agents/)\n613-            2. Compare agent definitions for consistency\n614-            3. Set scope = all discovered agent files\n615-          track: |\n616-            1. List all child spec folders under specs/{track}/ or .opencode/specs/{track}/\n--\n720:      step_create_state_log:\n721-        action: \"Open the run in the ledger: record deep_review.run_initialized through the append gateway, which writes the state log's first row\"\n722-        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n723-        note: |\n724-          The state log is a projection the gateway rebuilds from the ledger, so this step never writes\n725-          it directly. A config row written beside the ledger carries keys the projection cannot\n726-          rebuild, and the projection refuses to drop them, so every later append in the run would\n727-          commit to the ledger and then exit 2. Recording the run's opening as a ledger event makes\n728-          the projected config row the state log's first row from the start. The full config stays\n729-          in deep-review-config.json, which is what the reducer reads.\n730-        command: |\n731-          GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n732-          [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n733-          EVENT_FILE=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-run-open.XXXXXX\")\"\n734-          node -e '\n735-            const fs = require(\"fs\"), crypto = require(\"crypto\");\n736-            const [configPath, workflowPath] = process.argv.slice(1);\n737-            const sha = (bytes) => crypto.createHash(\"sha256\").update(bytes).digest(\"hex\");\n738-            const raw = fs.readFileSync(configPath);\n739-            const config = JSON.parse(raw);\n740-            const targetTypes = { files: \"file\", file: \"file\", directory: \"directory\", \"spec-folder\": \"directory\", track: \"directory\", repository: \"repository\" };\n741-            const lineageModes = { new: \"fresh\", fresh: \"fresh\", restart: \"restart\", resume: \"resume\" };\n742-            // The projected config row shows this topic; one the schema cannot hold is left out,\n743-            // and the row falls back to the run id rather than the run failing to open.\n744-            const topic = typeof config.topic === \"string\" && config.topic.trim() !== \"\" && config.topic.length <= 4096\n745-              ? config.topic\n746-              : null;\n747-            process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify({\n748-              stem: \"deep_review.run_initialized\",\n749-              scope: { runId: config.sessionId, sessionId: config.sessionId, generation: Number(config.generation) || 1 },\n750-              data: {\n751-                target: {\n752-                  targetId: \"review-target\",\n753-                  targetType: targetTypes[config.reviewTargetType] || \"artifact\",\n754-                  artifactRef: \"deep-review-config.json#reviewTarget\",\n755-                  sourceDigest: sha(String(config.reviewTarget)),\n756-                  contentDigest: sha(raw),\n757-                },\n758-                lineageMode: lineageModes[config.lineageMode] || \"fresh\",\n759-                maxIterations: Number(config.maxIterations),\n760-                convergencePolicyVersion: \"convergence-policy@\" + ((config.antiConvergence && config.antiConvergence.convergenceMode) || \"default\"),\n761-                reviewModeContractDigest: sha(fs.readFileSync(workflowPath)),\n762-                initialReleaseReadinessState: \"not-assessed\",\n763-                ...(topic === null ? {} : { topic }),\n764-              },\n765-            }));\n766-          ' \"{state_paths.config}\" \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml\" > \"$EVENT_FILE\" || { rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"; exit 1; }\n767-          node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n768-          STATUS=$?\n769-          rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n770-          exit \"$STATUS\"\n771-        output: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n772-\n773-      step_record_restarted_run:\n774-        skip_when: \"lineage_mode != 'restart'\"\n775-        action: \"Record the restarted lineage after the run-open row so the restart marker never precedes deep_review.run_initialized\"\n776-        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n777-        append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.run_restarted\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}},\"data\":{\"priorTailDigest\":\"{prior_tail_digest}\",\"archivedLineageId\":\"{prior_session_id}\",\"restartReason\":\"Restart requested: the prior review packet was archived and a new lineage segment opened.\",\"continuedFromRunId\":\"{prior_session_id}-i{iteration_count}\",\"compatibilityDecision\":\"exact\",\"recoveryReceiptRef\":\"none\"}}'\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"step_create_state_log\\\" -A 60 .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml | head -120\"}"},"time":{"start":1794760634531,"end":1794760635734}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794760635746,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd9ffeEQ4EaGVDFSUKgQ","part":{"partID":"prt_1e011f1f3001Ql5xueqCOL9nc7","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd9ffeEQ4EaGVDFSUKgQ","messageID":"msg_1e011e3180017Qq9TyOxRdMBIB","type":"tool","id":"call_7ccbeafe981445bb8ccfa58d","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"step_reduce_state\\|step_synthesis\\|step_update_config_status\\|step_save_continuity\" -A 40 .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml | head -200"},"output":"2074:      step_update_config_status:\n2075-        action: \"Mark config as complete\"\n2076-        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2077-        edit: \"{state_paths.config}\"\n2078-        set_field: { status: \"complete\" }\n2079-\n2080-      step_stage_artifact_dir:\n2081-        skip_when: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is present\"\n2082-        action: \"Stage all skill-owned artifacts under artifact_dir for the operator's next git commit\"\n2083-        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2084-        command: \"git add {state_paths.artifact_dir}\"\n2085-        note: \"Staging the whole artifact_dir keeps the iteration trail (iterations/, deltas/, state.jsonl, strategy, findings-registry, and the report) together; the operator keeps commit authority and can `git restore --staged {path}` before committing. Failure is non-fatal -- log warning and continue.\"\n2086-        on_fail: \"Log warning. Do not block synthesis. The artifact_dir may be outside a git repo (e.g., temp test fixture) which is a valid case.\"\n2087-\n2088-      # ─── APPROVAL GATE: Post-Synthesis ───\n2089-      gate_post_synthesis:\n2090-        applies_to: confirm\n2091-        type: approval_gate\n2092-        purpose: \"Show review/review-report.md summary and get approval\"\n2093-        present: |\n2094-          ## Review Synthesis Complete\n2095-\n2096-          **review/review-report.md** has been compiled with findings from {iteration_count} iterations.\n2097-          **Verdict**: {verdict} | **hasAdvisories**: {has_advisories}\n2098-          **Active Findings**: P0={active_p0} P1={active_p1} P2={active_p2}\n2099-          **Dimension Coverage**: {dimension_coverage}\n2100-\n2101-          Review `{state_paths.review_output}` before deciding next steps.\n2102-\n2103-          Options:\n2104-          A) Approve and save to memory\n2105-          B) Generate remediation plan (creates action items for /speckit:plan)\n2106-          C) Request revisions to review/review-report.md\n2107-          D) Skip memory save\n2108-        wait_for: \"User response\"\n2109-        after_gate_refresh_lock: gate_defaults.after_gate_refresh_lock\n2110-        on_A: { proceed_to: phase_save }\n2111-        on_B: { action: \"Generate remediation plan section, then save to memory\", proceed_to: phase_save }\n2112-        on_C: { action: \"Apply user revisions\", return_to: gate_post_synthesis }\n2113-        on_D: { proceed_to: completion }\n2114-\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"2074:      step_update_config_status:\n2075-        action: \"Mark config as complete\"\n2076-        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2077-        edit: \"{state_paths.config}\"\n2078-        set_field: { status: \"complete\" }\n2079-\n2080-      step_stage_artifact_dir:\n2081-        skip_when: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is present\"\n2082-        action: \"Stage all skill-owned artifacts under artifact_dir for the operator's next git commit\"\n2083-        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2084-        command: \"git add {state_paths.artifact_dir}\"\n2085-        note: \"Staging the whole artifact_dir keeps the iteration trail (iterations/, deltas/, state.jsonl, strategy, findings-registry, and the report) together; the operator keeps commit authority and can `git restore --staged {path}` before committing. Failure is non-fatal -- log warning and continue.\"\n2086-        on_fail: \"Log warning. Do not block synthesis. The artifact_dir may be outside a git repo (e.g., temp test fixture) which is a valid case.\"\n2087-\n2088-      # ─── APPROVAL GATE: Post-Synthesis ───\n2089-      gate_post_synthesis:\n2090-        applies_to: confirm\n2091-        type: approval_gate\n2092-        purpose: \"Show review/review-report.md summary and get approval\"\n2093-        present: |\n2094-          ## Review Synthesis Complete\n2095-\n2096-          **review/review-report.md** has been compiled with findings from {iteration_count} iterations.\n2097-          **Verdict**: {verdict} | **hasAdvisories**: {has_advisories}\n2098-          **Active Findings**: P0={active_p0} P1={active_p1} P2={active_p2}\n2099-          **Dimension Coverage**: {dimension_coverage}\n2100-\n2101-          Review `{state_paths.review_output}` before deciding next steps.\n2102-\n2103-          Options:\n2104-          A) Approve and save to memory\n2105-          B) Generate remediation plan (creates action items for /speckit:plan)\n2106-          C) Request revisions to review/review-report.md\n2107-          D) Skip memory save\n2108-        wait_for: \"User response\"\n2109-        after_gate_refresh_lock: gate_defaults.after_gate_refresh_lock\n2110-        on_A: { proceed_to: phase_save }\n2111-        on_B: { action: \"Generate remediation plan section, then save to memory\", proceed_to: phase_save }\n2112-        on_C: { action: \"Apply user revisions\", return_to: gate_post_synthesis }\n2113-        on_D: { proceed_to: completion }\n2114-\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"step_reduce_state\\\\|step_synthesis\\\\|step_update_config_status\\\\|step_save_continuity\\\" -A 40 .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml | head -200\"}"},"time":{"start":1794760634867,"end":1794760635746}}}}
