{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794761147749,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd9ffeEQ4EaGVDFSUKgQ","part":{"id":"prt_1e019c565001pM5J8IkC46iQf4","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd9ffeEQ4EaGVDFSUKgQ","messageID":"msg_1e019a1e7001Pe896zE3SOR2kI","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"e30a06f279747ad002b6c62eefb100a14854ad24","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":1637,"output":642,"reasoning":21,"cache":{"read":152832,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794761149843,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd9ffeEQ4EaGVDFSUKgQ","part":{"id":"prt_1e019cd93001saLHyJIKcBCvDR","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd9ffeEQ4EaGVDFSUKgQ","messageID":"msg_1e019c569001MP7aebQdBqZiFX","type":"step-start","snapshot":"e30a06f279747ad002b6c62eefb100a14854ad24"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794761191874,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd9ffeEQ4EaGVDFSUKgQ","part":{"partID":"prt_1e019d884002WlxowPxCK37bG3","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd9ffeEQ4EaGVDFSUKgQ","messageID":"msg_1e019c569001MP7aebQdBqZiFX","type":"tool","id":"call_9debb2ca1dfd41a086c3712b","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Deep Review Strategy - Session Tracking\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nPersistent brain for the pass-five `accuracy-runner-5` review lineage. The lineage reviews the routing-accuracy capture and scoring surfaces only: the transcript scorer, the behaviour runner, the arena builder and the docs/tests that describe them. Every finding is P0/P1/P2 with file:line and a concrete input.\n\n### Usage\n\n- Init wrote the topic, dimensions, known context and boundaries below.\n- Each iteration reads Next Focus, reviews one dimension, updates the running counts and sets the next focus.\n- Mutability: mutable, updated by each iteration. Machine-owned blocks are between explicit markers.\n\n---\n\n## 2. TOPIC\n\nPass-five code review of the command-surfacing measurement harness: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs`, `run-command-behaviour.mjs`, `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs`, the two folder READMEs and the two vitest files the scope lists for this area. Review target is the spec folder `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`.\n\n---\n\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- [x] D1 Correctness, Logic errors, off-by-one, wrong return types, broken invariants\n- [x] D2 Security, Injection, auth bypass, secrets exposure, unsafe deserialization\n- [x] D3 Traceability, Spec/code alignment, checklist evidence, cross-reference integrity\n- [x] D4 Maintainability, Patterns, clarity, documentation quality, safe follow-on change cost\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- The `kill-switch-cli`, `vibe-hooks-doctor` and `docs-metadata` areas other lineages own in pass five.\n- The advisor's scoring quality itself (routing accuracy, fusion thresholds); this lineage reviews the harness that measures behaviour.\n- Any code change. The lineage reports findings only.\n- Holdout prompt text: never read, printed or quoted, at any point.\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- Convergence at `convergenceThreshold` 0.1 or `maxIterations` 4, whichever comes first.\n- A P0 finding halts the PASS claim but not the iteration loop.\n- Any write outside `review/lineages/accuracy-runner-5/` stops the lineage.\n\n---\n\n## 6. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n| Dimension | Verdict | Iteration | Summary |\n|-----------|---------|-----------|---------|\n| D1 Correctness | CONDITIONAL | 1 | Scorer misses in-place shell writes in the unsafe and loop-init checks; a quoted `COMMAND:` line counts as a start |\n| D2 Security | PASS | 2 | Holdout and dotenv guards hold on every path read; arena clone and containment checks are sound, with two advisory gaps |\n| D3 Traceability | CONDITIONAL | 3 | Two README claims contradict the code they describe; scope-list growth is undocumented |\n| D4 Maintainability | PASS | 4 | One dead/duplicated tally field and one duplicated label source, both advisory |\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 7. RUNNING FINDINGS\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- **P0 (Critical):** 0 active\n- **P1 (Major):** 1 active\n- **P2 (Minor):** 5 active\n- **Delta this iteration:** +0 P0, +0 P1, +1 P2\n\nFindings are tracked in `deep-review-findings-registry.json`; this block is the running summary each iteration refreshes.\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Direct import of the scorer's exported facts and a one-shot `node --input-type=module -e` probe turned a suspected counting gap into observed evidence (iteration 1).\n- Reading `TOOL_TABLES` next to `normalize` showed the Vibe row deliberately omits a skill tool, which ruled out several suspected Vibe counting defects (iteration 1).\n- Grepping the packet's prior findings registry before writing avoided re-reporting four already-recorded README defects (iterations 1-4).\n- Reading the arena builder's destination checks against its own header comment found the two advisory gaps the tests do not cover (iteration 2).\n- Comparing each README sentence against the code it names found the two traceability defects cheaply (iteration 3).\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- Treating `firstWritePosition(stream)` and `firstWritePosition(stream, checkoutDir)` as interchangeable: the missing checkout argument in `startState` narrowed the diff to a scratch-path edge, not the real gap (iteration 1).\n- Expecting the runner's `--set chat` probe filter to require `split: tune`: every must-not-start row is split `none`, so filtering by `tune` would empty the bucket and no holdout row carries that row type, which left nothing actionable (iteration 2).\n- Looking for a Vibe multi-turn miscount: the runner mints a fresh session id per row, so multi-turn sessions are out of reach (iteration 2).\n- Trying to reconcile the README's file-count statistics: pass-two and pass-four already recorded that drift, and the structure table is generated prose rather than a claim about behaviour (iteration 3).\n\n---\n\n## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n\n### Transcript-counting gaps in `unsafe` -- PRODUCTIVE (iteration 1)\n- What worked: comparing the tool-name table and the redirect scan against every shell action that changes a file, then proving the gap by importing `normalize`/`startState`/`loopInit`.\n- Prefer for: any further question about what the scorer counts as a write, a load or a start.\n\n### Documented-claim drift in `routing-accuracy/README.md` -- BLOCKED (iterations 3-4, 2 attempts)\n- What was tried: every sentence in the README that describes scorer or runner behaviour was matched to the code; four separate drifts were found already recorded by pass two and pass four, so only the two new ones were reported.\n- Why blocked: the remaining sentences are accurate or already recorded; further passes would restate prior findings.\n- Do NOT retry: README structure-table statistics, backfill field counts, `--brief-only`, `--row-id` scope, paired-block wording.\n\n### Vibe journal scoring -- BLOCKED (iteration 2, 2 attempts)\n- What was tried: traced `loadVibeSession` -> `vibeRecords` -> `normalize('vibe')`, checked the table's tool names against the reader's journal records, and checked session scoping.\n- Why blocked: the tool names match the journal's recorded names, the missing skill tool is documented as deliberate, and the runner mints one session per row so multi-turn projections are out of reach.\n- Do NOT retry: Vibe tool-name coverage or Vibe turn scoping.\n\n---\n\n## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Swept: correctness, security, traceability, maintainability\n- Pivot lineage: none (single-lineage pass-five area review)\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n\n- `latestLines` collapsing two same-arm captures: the dedup is the documented retry rule and the key already lowers the count honestly; a second file with the same run number is an operator error the record cannot distinguish (iteration 1, evidence: `score-command-transcripts.mjs` `latestLines`).\n- `--set chat` probe bucket missing a `split` filter: no holdout row carries `row_type: must-not-start`, and `lookupPrompt` refuses a holdout id before the turn starts (iteration 2, evidence: corpus split/row_type counts, `findRow`).\n- Arena builder copying a tracked dotenv file: no dotenv file is tracked in this repository; only `.env.example` files are (iteration 2, evidence: `git ls-files`).\n- Vibe skill-tool blindness: documented in the tool table comment as a deliberate wait for a recorded name (iteration 2, evidence: `TOOL_TABLES.vibe`).\n- `derivePolicy` order versus the command-bridges README table: they agree step for step (iteration 3, evidence: `derive-command-bridges.cjs` `derivePolicy`).\n- `workflow.unscored` duplicating the block's unscored count: the field reads the same number and names it where the workflow block prints, so no reader is misled (iteration 4, evidence: `tallyBlock`).\n\n---\n\n## 12. NEXT FOCUS\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- Dimension: maintainability (complete); synthesis next\n- Focus area: none -- all four dimensions are covered and the loop stops at `maxIterations` 4\n- Reason: no dimension remains; the terminal stop is `maxIterationsReached`\n- Rotation status: swept\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: README drift and Vibe scoring are blocked; transcript-counting gaps are productive but exhausted\n- Required evidence: none outstanding\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\n\n- Target pointers: `score-command-transcripts.mjs` (2276 lines, scorer facts exported for tests), `run-command-behaviour.mjs` (1502 lines, live-turn runner), `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs` (354 lines, arena builder), `routing-accuracy/README.md`, `command-bridges/README.md`, `runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts`, `runtime/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts`.\n- Behaviour claims to verify: the scorer reports offer/start/follow counts per arm; `unsafe` covers a write on an `ask` row or a must-not-start row and a self-chosen `:auto`; loop starts are checked against their init; holdout rows are never scored, printed or run; the arena carries no dotenv file and no git remote.\n- Reuse and conventions: `TOOL_TABLES` is per runtime; `normalize` flattens records to `{seq,kind,path,command,text}`; `workflowPath`/`startState`/`loopInit` are exported and unit-tested; every refusal carries a stable `code`.\n- Review risks and gaps: the packet holds four prior lineages' findings for the same files, so deduplication against the registry is mandatory; holdout prompt text must never be read or printed; the loop's own state files are outside the write surface except the lineage directory.\n\n---\n\n## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n|----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\n| `spec_code` | core | pass | 3 | The scope list's area assignment matches the seven files reviewed; the changed files are the pass-four fix set |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pass | 3 | Each README claim reviewed was checked against the code it names; two drifts recorded |\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pass | 3 | The scorer and runner are consumed by `system-skill-advisor`'s runtime; no agent definition change in scope |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | notApplicable | 3 | No agent file is in this area's scope |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | partial | 3 | `docs-metadata` owns the feature-catalog pages; only the folder READMEs were cross-checked here |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | 3 | The manual-testing playbook is another lineage's area |\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n| File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\n|------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs` | D1, D2, D4 | 4 | 0 P0, 1 P1, 1 P2 | complete |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs` | D1, D2 | 2 | 0 P0, 0 P1, 1 P2 | complete |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs` | D2, D3 | 2 | 0 P0, 0 P1, 1 P2 | complete |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md` | D3, D4 | 3 | 0 P0, 0 P1, 2 P2 | complete |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md` | D3 | 3 | 0 P0, 0 P1, 0 P2 | complete |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` | D1, D4 | 4 | 0 P0, 0 P1, 1 P2 | complete |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` | D2, D3 | 2 | 0 P0, 0 P1, 1 P2 | complete |\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 16. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- Max iterations: 4\n- Convergence threshold: 0.1\n- Rolling STOP threshold: 0.08\n- No-progress threshold: 0.05\n- Coverage stabilization passes required: 1\n- Session lineage: sessionId=fanout-accuracy-runner-5-1794760565927-i99t40, parentSessionId=null, generation=1, lineageMode=new\n- Findings registry: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`\n- Release-readiness states: in-progress | converged | release-blocking\n- Per-iteration budget: 12 tool calls, 10 minutes\n- Severity threshold: P2\n- Review target type: spec-folder\n- Cross-reference checks: core=[spec_code, checklist_evidence], overlay=[skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, playbook_capability]\n- Started: 2026-11-15T16:45:21Z\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-5/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-5/deep-review-strategy.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-5/deep-review-strategy.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Deep Review Strategy - Session Tracking\\n\\n## 1. OVERVIEW\\n\\n### Purpos