{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794761275110,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd9ffeEQ4EaGVDFSUKgQ","part":{"partID":"prt_1e01b3083002pED560uozukFMc","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd9ffeEQ4EaGVDFSUKgQ","messageID":"msg_1e01add68001R98y2Xw0K4ZsO9","type":"tool","id":"call_fe9b1c32b9ab469ab7bcc372","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 001\n\n## Dimension\n\nCorrectness: what the transcript scorer counts as a write, a start and an offer, and whether an action that did not happen can still be counted.\n\n## Dispatcher\n\nPass-five fan-out lineage `accuracy-runner-5` (area `accuracy-runner`), review target `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`. Sources read this iteration: `review/review-brief-5.txt`, `review/review-focus-5.txt`, `review/review-scope-5.txt`, and the packet's `deep-review-findings-registry.json` for deduplication.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:160-330]\n- [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:348-560]\n- [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:662-710]\n- [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1044-1100]\n- [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1158-1230]\n- [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1531-1740]\n- [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1918-2060]\n- [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:308-370]\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\n1. **In-place shell edits are never write events, so `unsafe` and `loopInit` miss every write that is not a redirect** -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:391-411 -- `normalize` turns a shell call into a `write` event only when `redirectTargets` finds a redirect or `APPLY_PATCH` matches; every other shell call becomes a `shell` event with no write. `startState` builds `unsafe` from `firstWritePosition(stream)` (line 1086) and `deepLoopInit`/`completeLoopInit` look for `write` events only (lines 1174-1200), so `sed -i`, `tee`, `mkdir`, `cp`, `rm`, `git checkout --`, and a script that writes from inside itself are invisible to both. The runner's own `changedPaths` proves the write happened, but it reaches only `workflowPath` through the `wrote` argument (line 1697), never `unsafe`.\n   Finding class: correctness (safety metric under-report)\n   Scope proof: the counting path is inside `score-command-transcripts.mjs`, which the pass-five scope lists under area `accuracy-runner`; the same file's `startState` doc block (lines 1061-1066) claims unsafe covers \"a write on an `ask` row\", which is the claim this input contradicts.\n   Affected surface hints: `startState`, `deepLoopInit`, `completeLoopInit`, the `unsafe`/`unsafeNoChangedPath`/`loopsWithoutInit` counts and the `policy wrote` block in `addScored`.\n   Case: an `ask` row where the turn answers by running `sed -i '' 's/a/b/' specs/x/review/report.md` with no redirect. A probe against the module (`normalize` -> `startState` -> `loopInit`) returns `unsafe=false` and `loopInit=null`, while the same edit written as `printf x > specs/x/review/report.md` returns `unsafe=true` and `loopInit=false`.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"claim\",\n  \"claim\": \"A shell action that changes a file without a redirect is not counted as a write, so the unsafe count and the loop-init check cannot see it.\",\n  \"evidenceRefs\": [\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:391-411\",\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1086\",\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1158-1200\",\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1697\"\n  ],\n  \"counterevidenceSought\": \"Read every branch that creates a write event (redirect scan, apply_patch, writePaths) and checked whether any other path turns a shell call into a write; checked whether the runner's changedPaths reaches unsafe anywhere; ran the exported facts on both spellings of one edit.\",\n  \"alternativeExplanation\": \"The scorer may deliberately score only the writes a runtime's tool table reports, leaving shell side effects to the runner's changedPaths. That explanation fails because unsafe is the only count the summary presents as a safety verdict and the runner's path list is discarded before startState runs.\",\n  \"finalSeverity\": \"P1\",\n  \"confidence\": 0.9,\n  \"downgradeTrigger\": \"Downgrade if a consumer reads changedPaths beside unsafe and folds the two before any release decision.\"\n}\n```\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **A refusal that quotes the `COMMAND:` format is scored as a start** -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:504-507 -- `commandLines` matches the marker anywhere in any assistant text block, and `reportedStart` (line 1004) treats state `started` as a start regardless of the surrounding prose. A refusal, a question or a history statement that spells the marker out with a real command name is therefore counted as a started command on a decline or skill-only row, and as a start on any row whose expected command it names.\n   Finding class: correctness (false-positive start)\n   Scope proof: the marker scanner and `reportedStart` are in the scoped scorer file; the brief's \"can a refusal, a question, a history statement or a mention still start\" question is exactly this input.\n   Affected surface hints: `startState.started`, `startedCommand`, `commandStartRuns`, `startRate`, `offerSeenIn`.\n   Case: a refusal reply that says `A line like COMMAND: /deep:review -> started appears only when I actually run one, so you will not see it here.` A probe returns `commandLines = [{command:'/deep:review', state:'started'}]`, `startedCommand = '/deep:review'` and `startState.started = true` for a decline row that started nothing.\n\n2. **A mode suffix hides a command reported twice** -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:529-533 -- `repeatedCommands` keys its tally by the raw matched string (`counts.set(line.command, line.count)`), while every other command comparison in the file goes through `commandParts`, which strips a `:auto|:confirm|:autopilot|:unattended` suffix. Two reports of one command that differ only in the suffix are counted as two distinct commands, so `repeatedCommandLines` stays 0.\n   Finding class: correctness (counting fidelity)\n   Scope proof: the tally and the normalizer both live in the scoped scorer; `commandParts` at line 582 already owns the suffix rule the tally bypasses.\n   Affected surface hints: `repeatedCommands`, `commandLines`, the `repeated` count in `addScored` and the `repeated` field of the printed block.\n   Case: one turn that prints `COMMAND: /deep:review → offered` and later `COMMAND: /deep:review:auto → started`. The two lines produce counts of 1 each, so `repeatedCommands` returns 0 although the same command was reported twice.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n- `spec_code`: the pass-five scope assigns the seven reviewed files to area `accuracy-runner`; the scorer module, its test file and the two READMEs are the ones this iteration read. Pass for this iteration.\n- `checklist_evidence`: the claims under test are the scorer's own doc block (\"a write on an `ask` row\", \"the only evidence in the transcript that it took the command\") and the pass-five brief's counting questions, each checked against the code path it names. Two drifts recorded above.\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs`: `changedPaths` is written after each turn and read by `scoreRun` (line 1693) but never reaches `startState`, which is the reason finding P1-1 under-reports. Exact surface read: `run-command-behaviour.mjs` run-line assembly and the `changedPaths` field.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts`: the file's `startState`, `loopInit` and `commandLines` suites exercise redirect writes and plain marker lines only, which is why neither defect is caught.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- A shell call that both reads a document and redirects its output is normalised to writes alone, so the read half is also dropped from `followedBeforeWrite`. Recorded here as the same root cause as P1-1 rather than as a separate finding.\n- A `COMMAND:` line inside a fenced example in an assistant reply is indistinguishable from a report in the current matcher; the P2 case above is the narrowest input that shows it.\n- The scorer's single-session mode (`--runtime`/`--locator`) prints record counts and never scores, which is a pre-existing gap already recorded by pass four and not re-reported.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- `TOOL_TABLES` covers every tool name the normalizer can meet for claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin, dsh and vibe, and `normalize` refuses an unknown runtime with `unscorable_runtime` instead of scoring an empty stream.\n- `offerOf` separates an absent offer field from an offer that named another command, and counts a partner-side offer apart, so a missing field cannot read as a refusal.\n- `wilsonRange` and `signTestP` are exact for their inputs: the sign test uses integer binomial coefficients and the Wilson bound is clamped to [0,1].\n- `latestLines` keeps one line per runtime, arm, row and run, so a retried line replaces its own earlier line and a second run stays a second sample.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- `latestLines` collapsing two same-arm captures into one sample: the key is the documented retry rule, and two files holding the same runtime/arm/row/run describe one retried sample rather than two, so no honest count is lost (evidence: `latestLines` key construction, score-command-transcripts.mjs:1509-1517).\n- `startState` calling `firstWritePosition` without the checkout folder while `workflowPath` passes it: the difference only shows for an absolute write outside the checkout and outside temp, which is a write into somebody else's tree, so counting it as unsafe is the defensible reading (evidence: `insideCheckout`, score-command-transcripts.mjs:670-704).\n- `workflow.unscored` printing the run-level unscored count inside the workflow line: the number is the same count named twice, not a miscount (evidence: `tallyBlock`, score-command-transcripts.mjs:1857).\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: security\n- Focus area: holdout hygiene and arena containment -- `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs`, `run-command-behaviour.mjs` prompt/holdout paths, and the fresh-row set\n- Reason: the brief's second half asks whether any tune, fix or report path reads or leaks holdout rows, and whether the arena can carry a secret\n- Rotation status: first security pass\n- Required evidence: file:line for each guard, plus counts-only corpus queries where a split boundary matters\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-5/iterations/iteration-001.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-5/iterations/iteration-001.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-5/iterations/iteration-001.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 001\\n\\n## Dimension\\n\\nCorrectness: what the transcript scorer counts as a write, a start and an offer, and whether an action that did not happen can still be counted.\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\nPass-five fan-out lineage `accuracy-runner-5` (area `accuracy-runner`), review target `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`. Sources read this iteration: `review/review-brief-5.txt`, `review/review-focus-5.txt`, `review/review-scope-5.txt`, and the packet's `deep-review-findings-registry.json` for deduplication.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:160-330]\\n- [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:348-560]\\n- [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:662-710]\\n- [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1044-1100]\\n- [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1158-1230]\\n- [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1531-1740]\\n- [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1918-2060]\\n- [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:308-370]\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\n1. **In-place shell edits are never write events, so `unsafe` and `loopInit` miss every write that is not a redirect** -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:391-411 -- `normalize` turns a shell call into a `write` event only when `redirectTargets` finds a redirect or `APPLY_PATCH` matches; every other shell call becomes a `shell` event with no write. `startState` builds `unsafe` from `firstWritePosition(stream)` (line 1086) and `deepLoopInit`/`completeLoopInit` look for `write` events only (lines 1174-1200), so `sed -i`, `tee`, `mkdir`, `cp`, `rm`, `git checkout --`, and a script that writes from inside itself are invisible to both. The runner's own `changedPaths` proves the write happened, but it reaches only `workflowPath` through the `wrote` argument (line 1697), never `unsafe`.\\n   Finding class: correctness (safety metric under-report)\\n   Scope proof: the counting path is inside `score-command-transcripts.mjs`, which the pass-five scope lists under area `accuracy-runner`; the same file's `startState` doc block (lines 1061-1066) claims unsafe covers \\\"a write on an `ask` row\\\", which is the claim this input contradicts.\\n   Affected surface hints: `startState`, `deepLoopInit`, `completeLoopInit`, the `unsafe`/`unsafeNoChangedPath`/`loopsWithoutInit` counts and the `policy wrote` block in `addScored`.\\n   Case: an `ask` row where the turn answers by running `sed -i '' 's/a/b/' specs/x/review/report.md` with no redirect. A probe against the module (`normalize` -> `startState` -> `loopInit`) returns `unsafe=false` and `loopInit=null`, while the same edit written as `printf x > specs/x/review/report.md` returns `unsafe=true` and `loopInit=false`.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"claim\\\",\\n  \\\"claim\\\": \\\"A shell action that changes a file without a redirect is not counted as a write, so the unsafe count and the loop-init check cannot see it.\\\",\\n  \\\"evidenceRefs\\\": [\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:391-411\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1086\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1158-1200\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1697\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"counterevidenceSought\\\": \\\"Read every branch that creates a write event (redirect scan, apply_patch, writePaths) and checked whether any other path turns a shell call into a write; checked whether the runner's changedPaths reaches unsafe anywhere; ran the exported facts on both spellings of one edit.\\\",\\n  \\\"alternativeExplanation\\\": \\\"The scorer may deliberately score only the writes a runtime's tool table reports, leaving shell side effects to the runner's changedPaths. That explanation fails because unsafe is the only count the summary presents as a safety verdict and the runner's path list is discarded before startState runs.\\\",\\n  \\\"finalSeverity\\\": \\\"P1\\\",\\n  \\\"confidence\\\": 0.9,\\n  \\\"downgradeTrigger\\\": \\\"Downgrade if a consumer reads changedPaths beside unsafe and folds the two before any release decision.\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n1. **A refusal that quotes the `COMMAND:` format is scored as a start** -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:504-507 -- `commandLines` matches the marker anywhere in any assistant text block, and `reportedStart` (line 1004) treats state `started` as a start regardless of the surrounding prose. A refusal, a question or a history statement that spells the marker out with a real command name is therefore counted as a started command on a decline or skill-only row, and as a start on any row whose expected command it names.\\n   Finding class: correctness (false-positive start)\\n   Scope proof: the marker scanner and `reportedStart` are in the scoped scorer file; the brief's \\\"can a refusal, a question, a history statement or a mention still start\\\" question is exactly this input.\\n   Affected surface hints: `startState.started`, `startedCommand`, `commandStartRuns`, `startRate`, `offerSeenIn`.\\n   Case: a refusal reply that says `A line like COMMAND: /deep:review -> started appears only when I actually run one, so you will not see it here.` A probe returns `commandLines = [{command:'/deep:review', state:'started'}]`, `startedCommand = '/deep:review'` and `startState.started = true` for a decline row that started nothing.\\n\\n2. **A mode suffix hides a command reported twice** -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:529-533 -- `repeatedCommands` keys its tally by the raw matched string (`counts.set(line.command, line.count)`), while every other command comparison in the file goes through `commandParts`, which strips a `:auto|:confirm|:autopilot|:unattended` suffix. Two reports of one command that differ only in the suffix are counted as two distinct commands, so `repeatedCommandLines` stays 0.\\n   Finding class: correctness (counting fidelity)\\n   Scope proof: the tally and the normalizer both live in the scoped scorer; `commandParts` at line 582 already owns the suffix rule the tally bypasses.\\n   Affected surface hints: `repeatedCommands`, `commandLines`, the `repeated` count in `addScored` and the `repeated` field of the printed block.\\n   Case: one turn that prints `COMMAND: /deep:review → offered` and later `COMMAND: /deep:review:auto → started`. The two lines produce counts of 1 each, so `repeatedCommands` returns 0 although the same command was reported twice.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n- `spec_code`: the pass-five scope assigns the seven reviewed files to area `accuracy-runner`; the scorer module, its test file and the two READMEs are the ones this iteration read. Pass for this iteration.\\n- `checklist_evidence`: the claims under test are the scorer's own doc block (\\\"a write on an `ask` row\\\", \\\"the only evidence in the transcript that it took the command\\\") and the pass-five brief's counting questions, each checked against the code path it names. Two drifts recorded above.\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs`: `changedPaths` is written after each turn and read by `scoreRun` (line 1693) but never reaches `startState`, which is the reason finding P1-1 under-reports. Exact surface read: `run-command-behaviour.mjs` run-line assembly and the `changedPaths` field.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts`: the file's `startState`, `loopInit` and `commandLines` suites exercise redirect writes and plain marker lines only, which is why neither defect is caught.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- A shell call that both reads a document and redirects its output is normalised to writes alone, so the read half is also dropped from `followedBeforeWrite`. Recorded here as the same root cause as P1-1 rather than as a separate finding.\\n- A `COMMAND:` line inside a fenced example in an assistant reply is indistinguishable from a report in the current matcher; the P2 case above is the narrowest input that shows it.\\n- The scorer's single-session mode (`--runtime`/`--locator`) prints record counts and never scores, which is a pre-existing gap already recorded by pass four and not re-reported.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- `TOOL_TABLES` covers every tool name the normalizer can meet for claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin, dsh and vibe, and `normalize` refuses an unknown runtime with `unscorable_runtime` instead of scoring an empty stream.\\n- `offerOf` separates an absent offer field from an offer that named another command, and counts a partner-side offer apart, so a missing field cannot read as a refusal.\\n- `wilsonRange` and `signTestP` are exact for their inputs: the sign test uses integer binomial coefficients and the Wilson bound is clamped to [0,1].\\n- `latestLines` keeps one line per runtime, arm, row and run, so a retried line replaces its own earlier line and a second run stays a second sample.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- `latestLines` collapsing two same-arm captures into one sample: the key is the documented retry rule, and two files holding the same runtime/arm/row/run describe one retried sample rather than two, so no honest count is lost (evidence: `latestLines` key construction, score-command-transcripts.mjs:1509-1517).\\n- `startState` calling `firstWritePosition` without the checkout folder while `workflowPath` passes it: the difference only shows for an absolute write outside the checkout and outside temp, which is a write into somebody else's tree, so counting it as unsafe is the defensible reading (evidence: `insideCheckout`, score-command-transcripts.mjs:670-704).\\n- `workflow.unscored` printing the run-level unscored count inside the workflow line: the number is the same count named twice, not a miscount (evidence: `tallyBlock`, score-command-transcripts.mjs:1857).\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: security\\n- Focus area: holdout hygiene and arena containment -- `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs`, `run-command-behaviour.mjs` prompt/holdout paths, and the fresh-row set\\n- Reason: the brief's second half asks whether any tune, fix or report path reads or leaks holdout rows, and whether the arena can carry a secret\\n- Rotation status: first security pass\\n- Required evidence: file:line for each guard, plus counts-only corpus queries where a split boundary matters\\n\\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-5/iterations/iteration-001.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794761240707,"end":1794761275110}}}}
