{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794761346499,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd9ffeEQ4EaGVDFSUKgQ","part":{"partID":"prt_1e01cae15002fzX1I77LEco1OH","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd9ffeEQ4EaGVDFSUKgQ","messageID":"msg_1e01ca6150018sq2BOHZ2BnbEJ","type":"tool","id":"call_4c4713f2c39c490c9c882978","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"- `latestLines` collapsing two same-arm captures into one sample: the key is the documented retry rule, and two files holding the same runtime/arm/row/run describe one retried sample rather than two, so no honest count is lost (iteration 1, evidence: `latestLines`, score-command-transcripts.mjs:1509-1517).\n- `startState` calling `firstWritePosition` without the checkout folder while `workflowPath` passes it: the difference only shows for an absolute write outside the checkout and outside temp, which is a write into somebody else's tree, so counting it as unsafe is the defensible reading (iteration 1, evidence: `insideCheckout`, score-command-transcripts.mjs:670-704).\n- `workflow.unscored` printing the run-level unscored count inside the workflow line: the same count is named twice, not miscounted (iteration 1, evidence: `tallyBlock`, score-command-transcripts.mjs:1857).","oldString":"[Populated as directions are investigated and eliminated]","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-5/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-5/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-5/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-5/deep-review-strategy.md\n============================================