{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794761609452,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd9ffeEQ4EaGVDFSUKgQ","part":{"id":"prt_1e020d0ec0014bVuerVl5fP6Rk","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd9ffeEQ4EaGVDFSUKgQ","messageID":"msg_1e020c830001t74bsHFXBsFum4","type":"step-start","snapshot":"61ba4da581e50173edc85896300c6b2e592e6e1e"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794761610428,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd9ffeEQ4EaGVDFSUKgQ","part":{"partID":"prt_1e020d33d001w5FaoKe5EJG9be","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd9ffeEQ4EaGVDFSUKgQ","messageID":"msg_1e020c830001t74bsHFXBsFum4","type":"tool","id":"call_22f9dd58e3824e10ac20ee90","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-5/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-5/deep-review-strategy.md, lines 1-168\n1: # Deep Review Strategy - Session Tracking\n2: \n3: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n4: \n5: ### Purpose\n6: \n7: Persistent brain for the pass-five `accuracy-runner-5` review lineage. The lineage reviews the routing-accuracy capture and scoring surfaces only: the transcript scorer, the behaviour runner, the arena builder and the docs/tests that describe them. Every finding is P0/P1/P2 with file:line and a concrete input.\n8: \n9: ### Usage\n10: \n11: - Init wrote the topic, dimensions, known context and boundaries below.\n12: - Each iteration reads Next Focus, reviews one dimension, updates the running counts and sets the next focus.\n13: - Mutability: mutable, updated by each iteration. Machine-owned blocks are between explicit markers.\n14: \n15: ---\n16: \n17: ## 2. TOPIC\n18: \n19: Pass-five code review of the command-surfacing measurement harness: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs`, `run-command-behaviour.mjs`, `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs`, the two folder READMEs and the two vitest files the pass-five scope lists for this area. Review target is the spec folder `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`.\n20: \n21: ---\n22: \n23: <!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n24: ## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n25: - [ ] security\n26: - [ ] traceability\n27: - [ ] maintainability\n28: \n29: <!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n30: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n31: \n32: - The `kill-switch-cli`, `vibe-hooks-doctor` and `docs-metadata` areas other lineages own in pass five.\n33: - The advisor's scoring quality itself (routing accuracy, fusion thresholds); this lineage reviews the harness that measures behaviour.\n34: - Any code change. The lineage reports findings only.\n35: - Holdout prompt text: never read, printed or quoted, at any point.\n36: \n37: ---\n38: \n39: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n40: \n41: - Convergence at `convergenceThreshold` 0.1 or `maxIterations` 4, whichever comes first.\n42: - A P0 finding halts the PASS claim but not the iteration loop.\n43: - Any write outside `review/lineages/accuracy-runner-5/` stops the lineage.\n44: \n45: ---\n46: \n47: <!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n48: ## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n49: - [x] correctness\n50: \n51: <!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n52: <!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n53: ## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n54: - P0 (Blockers): 0\n55: - P1 (Required): 1\n56: - P2 (Suggestions): 2\n57: - Resolved: 0\n58: \n59: <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n60: ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n61: \n62: - Direct import of the scorer's exported facts and a one-shot `node --input-type=module -e` probe turned two suspected counting gaps into observed evidence instead of inference (iteration 1).\n63: - Comparing the write-event producers (`redirectTargets`, `APPLY_PATCH`, `writePaths`) against every shell action that changes a file isolated the invisible-write class in one read (iteration 1).\n64: \n65: ---\n66: \n67: ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n68: \n69: - Treating `firstWritePosition(stream)` and `firstWritePosition(stream, checkoutDir)` as interchangeable: the missing checkout argument narrowed to a scratch-path edge and was ruled out, while the real gap was the absent write event (iteration 1).\n70: - Expecting `workflow.unscored` to be a workflow-path count: it reads the run-level unscored count and only names it again (iteration 1).\n71: \n72: ---\n73: \n74: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n75: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n76: ### `latestLines` collapsing two same-arm captures into one sample: the key is the documented retry rule, and two files holding the same runtime/arm/row/run describe one retried sample rather than two, so no honest count is lost (evidence: `latestLines` key construction, score-command-transcripts.mjs:1509-1517). -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n77: - What was tried: `latestLines` collapsing two same-arm captures into one sample: the key is the documented retry rule, and two files holding the same runtime/arm/row/run describe one retried sample rather than two, so no honest count is lost (evidence: `latestLines` key construction, score-command-transcripts.mjs:1509-1517).\n78: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n79: - Do NOT retry: `latestLines` collapsing two same-arm captures into one sample: the key is the documented retry rule, and two files holding the same runtime/arm/row/run describe one retried sample rather than two, so no honest count is lost (evidence: `latestLines` key construction, score-command-transcripts.mjs:1509-1517).\n80: \n81: ### `startState` calling `firstWritePosition` without the checkout folder while `workflowPath` passes it: the difference only shows for an absolute write outside the checkout and outside temp, which is a write into somebody else's tree, so counting it as unsafe is the defensible reading (evidence: `insideCheckout`, score-command-transcripts.mjs:670-704). -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n82: - What was tried: `startState` calling `firstWritePosition` without the checkout folder while `workflowPath` passes it: the difference only shows for an absolute write outside the checkout and outside temp, which is a write into somebody else's tree, so counting it as unsafe is the defensible reading (evidence: `insideCheckout`, score-command-transcripts.mjs:670-704).\n83: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n84: - Do NOT retry: `startState` calling `firstWritePosition` without the checkout folder while `workflowPath` passes it: the difference only shows for an absolute write outside the checkout and outside temp, which is a write into somebody else's tree, so counting it as unsafe is the defensible reading (evidence: `insideCheckout`, score-command-transcripts.mjs:670-704).\n85: \n86: ### `workflow.unscored` printing the run-level unscored count inside the workflow line: the number is the same count named twice, not a miscount (evidence: `tallyBlock`, score-command-transcripts.mjs:1857). -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n87: - What was tried: `workflow.unscored` printing the run-level unscored count inside the workflow line: the number is the same count named twice, not a miscount (evidence: `tallyBlock`, score-command-transcripts.mjs:1857).\n88: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n89: - Do NOT retry: `workflow.unscored` printing the run-level unscored count inside the workflow line: the number is the same count named twice, not a miscount (evidence: `tallyBlock`, score-command-transcripts.mjs:1857).\n90: \n91: <!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n92: ## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n93: - Completed pivots: 0\n94: - Failed pivots: 0\n95: - Audited overrides: 0\n96: - Swept: none yet\n97: - Pivot lineage: none yet\n98: - Remaining frontier: none recorded\n99: \n100: ## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n101: \n102: - `latestLines` collapsing two same-arm captures into one sample: the key is the documented retry rule, and two files holding the same runtime/arm/row/run describe one retried sample rather than two, so no honest count is lost (iteration 1, evidence: `latestLines`, score-command-transcripts.mjs:1509-1517).\n103: - `startState` calling `firstWritePosition` without the checkout folder while `workflowPath` passes it: the difference only shows for an absolute write outside the checkout and outside temp, which is a write into somebody else's tree, so counting it as unsafe is the defensible reading (iteration 1, evidence: `insideCheckout`, score-command-transcripts.mjs:670-704).\n104: - `workflow.unscored` printing the run-level unscored count inside the workflow line: the same count is named twice, not miscounted (iteration 1, evidence: `tallyBlock`, score-command-transcripts.mjs:1857).\n105: \n106: ---\n107: \n108: <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n109: ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n110: - Dimension: security - Focus area: holdout hygiene and arena containment -- `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs`, `run-command-behaviour.mjs` prompt/holdout paths, and the fresh-row set - Reason: the brief's second half asks whether any tune, fix or report path reads or leaks holdout rows, and whether the arena can carry a secret - Rotation status: first security pass - Required evidence: file:line for each guard, plus counts-only corpus queries where a split boundary matters Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\n111: \n112: <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n113: ## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n114: \n115: ### Bounded Context Snapshot\n116: \n117: - Target pointers: `score-command-transcripts.mjs` (2276 lines, scorer facts exported for tests), `run-command-behaviour.mjs` (1502 lines, live-turn runner), `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs` (354 lines, arena builder), `routing-accuracy/README.md`, `command-bridges/README.md`, `runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts`, `runtime/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts`.\n118: - Behaviour claims to verify: the scorer reports offer/start/follow counts per arm; `unsafe` covers a write on an `ask` row or a must-not-start row and a self-chosen `:auto`; loop starts are checked against their init; holdout rows are never scored, printed or run; the arena carries no dotenv file and no git remote.\n119: - Reuse and conventions: `TOOL_TABLES` is per runtime; `normalize` flattens records to `{seq,kind,path,command,text}`; `workflowPath`/`startState`/`loopInit` are exported and unit-tested; every refusal carries a stable `code`.\n120: - Review risks and gaps: the packet holds four prior lineages' findings for the same files, so deduplication against `deep-review-findings-registry.json` is mandatory; holdout prompt text must never be read or printed; the loop's own state files are outside the write surface except this lineage directory.\n121: \n122: ---\n123: \n124: ## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n125: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n126: | Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n127: |----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\n128: | `spec_code` | core | pending | - | - |\n129: | `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | - | - |\n130: | `skill_agent` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n131: | `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n132: | `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n133: | `playbook_capability` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n134: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n135: \n136: ---\n137: \n138: ## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\n139: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n140: | File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\n141: |------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\n142: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs` | D1 | 1 | 0 P0, 1 P1, 2 P2 | partial |\n143: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs` | - | - | - | pending |\n144: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs` | - | - | - | pending |\n145: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md` | - | - | - | pending |\n146: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md` | - | - | - | pending |\n147: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` | D1 | 1 | 